{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Behold, of the fatness of the land.</b> Part of the land of Israel, which is the fatness of the land." "<b>Shall be your dwelling.</b> This is Mount Seir, adjacent to the land of Israel, in the portion of Judah, and it is a fat land and watered by the dew of the heavens like the land of Israel. And whence do we know that the Holy One, blessed be He, agreed through him? As it is written: 'and I gave Esau Mount Seir.' 'Shall be your dwelling' — whether you merit or whether you do not merit, for if the matter depended on merit it would never come to pass; but concerning Israel it is written the attribute of justice, to teach you: if they merit. <br>"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "The phrase 'the attribute of justice' (מדת הדין) appears to be quoted or alluded to from a verse, but the text as given is abrupt and possibly defective; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:22.750984289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}